  ],
  "notes": "Critic revision. (1) FIXED ext.licence.class (critic wrong verdict): the cell is now emitted whole as one observation, no split, so compound classes such as 'Fire Detection, Alarm and Warning Systems - Occupational' and 'Glass, Glazing and Aluminium' stay intact. The static UNSPLIT_LIST_VALUES check remains unsatisfied by design - probing showed it is cleared only by a ', ' split that the critic demonstrated fabricates classes on held-out rows; correctness wins, flagged for the reviewer. (2) FIXED ext.financial.revenue_band (critic wrong verdict): rule removed; Financial Category CODE/DESC unmapped because QBCC's financial category is a licence financial-requirement/contract-value tier (SCT1 = 'Self Certification - Trade'), not a revenue/turnover band of the business, and the qbcc_mfr scheme is unverified. Nothing is emitted where the source does not state revenue. (3) KEPT ext.entity.industry_code from Licence Class Type via crosswalk anzsic_qbcc_licence_class (scheme anzsic2006), critic verdict 'doubtful': the direction (unsplit raw class -> ANZSIC via a crosswalk whose keys are these exact strings, 508/508 discovery and 1101/1101 held-out matches, zero errors) is right; the remaining doubt is the table's draft L2 status and that a licensed trade is arguably the business's performed activity for contractor grades (Trade Contractor Licence 462/508) but less so for supervisory/nominee grades (30/508) - left in place for human sign-off rather than dropped or self-written. (4) KEPT holder_kind, licence number/grade and HOLDS_LICENCE (all 'ok'). Approved rules 0-6 untouched. Note for the reviewer: Licence Number has 506 distinct/508 rows (two holders appear twice with the same number); the licence key is therefore not unique. No personal contact data is anywhere in the emitted claims."
}"}

